  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of the Integration of the Refugee Population into the Labour Market</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to facilitate beneficiaries&apos; integration in the local labor markets and societies through employment in sectors that present significant shortcomings in human resources. The main target group of the project will consist beneficiaries of international protection and third-country nationals legally residing in Greece, who will benefit from specialized and tailor-made support to successfully access the Greek labor market. To achieve the envisaged objective, the project is comprised of eight components. Each component focuses on a distinct field and aims to provide beneficiaries with quality training opportunities that will support them in secure employment. Two types of training will be available based on the nature of each component and the respective training area, namely the provision of traineeship or the provision of vocational training. Additionally, all components will encompass several other services to facilitate beneficiaries&apos; participation in the project and the successful completion of their training programs. Particularly, a skills assessment will be performed for all beneficiaries to get an insight into beneficiaries&apos; personal and professional profiles and guide them to select the areas in which they would like to train. Interpretation and Job counseling will also be offered throughout the project implementation offering comprehensive support to project beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
